  "details": "The ability to change controller (keyboard) button, joystick, and axis mapping on the fly in game. \n\nHaving to back out and \"SHIFT LAUNCH\" the game just to change UNITY MAPPING SETTINGS is less than ideal.\n\nI've experienced and noticed other players becoming frustrated with certain mappings and wished they could change, test, and confirm them in game.\n\nADDITIONAL FEATURES:\n\nThis would include the ability to bind buttons or key combinations for specific actions such as emotes, actions, and various Menu Functions.\n\nThese could be and are not limited to TARGET PLAYER: Mute, Block, Disable Avatar, Toggle Shaders, Invite, Friend, and etc.\n\nAs well as MENU ELEMENTS such as DROP PORTAL: New Instance, Favorite X, LOAD AVATAR X, and etc.\n\nQUALITY OF LIFE FEATURES:\n\nSome Desktop and VR players have limited use of limbs due to a disability. This includes limited arm, wrist, and hand movements, the loss of limbs or even underdeveloped ones. These players are looking to feel a sense of normalcy through the virtual space.\n\nAllowing VR or Desktop Players to use a mouse / keyboard, flightstick or gamepad to simulate motion controls would go a long way. This could work in a similar manner to Surgeon Simulator. Allowing players to use their own input methods to replicate motion controls. Hand rotation, grasping, gesture and etc.",
